  "narrative": {
   "care_continuity": [
    "National isolation/CTE stock: 833. The source prints no complete national capacity denominator.",
    "Ituri: 471 patients for 983 beds (47.9%); Nord-Kivu: 287 for 220 beds (130.5%); Haut-Uele: 49 for 134 beds (36.6%); Tshopo: 7 for 25 beds (28.0%); Sud-Kivu: 19 patients at a printed 76.0%, without a printed bed count.",
    "Every printed occupancy percentage agrees with its own printed patient and bed counts where both are supplied; Sud-Kivu's rate is retained without deriving an unprinted capacity denominator.",
    "Five provinces publish an isolation block. Bas-Uele reports no CTE/CT and no ambulance and publishes no occupancy block.",
    "Bas-Uele reports no CTE/CT and no ambulance and publishes no occupancy block; its values remain unset rather than inferred.",
    "The five reporting provinces sum to 833 exactly, matching the printed national stock with no unallocated residual."
   ],
   "challenges": [
    "The source records 2,140 alerts, 1,389 verified alerts (64.9%), 408 validated suspects, and 100% investigation of those suspects. The changing alert denominator remains a reporting-coverage series, not a transmission indicator.",
    "Care capacity: Nord-Kivu is at 287 patients against 220 beds (130.5% occupancy), above capacity for a sixth consecutive reviewed cut. In Ituri, Nizi, Mambasa Lolwa, Kilo, Mangala and Mandima are saturated for suspects. Pawa lacks hygiene installations; Isiro lacks space, water and permanent electricity; Tshopo lacks secure blood and a full technical platform; Bas-Uele lacks a CTE/CT and ambulance.",
    "Contact follow-up is 86.5% (21,723/25,108), above the 85% threshold nationally but below it in Nord-Kivu (84.3%), Tshopo (83.2%), Haut-Uele (76.9%) and Bas-Uele (71.1%). Sud-Kivu publishes no contact row. INSP attributes weak follow-up particularly to insufficient dedicated surveillance and contact-tracing teams in Bas-Uele.",
    "PoE/PoC report completeness is printed as 84.6% (99/117), while the five provincial component rows sum to 105/130 (80.8%). Both are preserved as a source conflict; the 100% strategic-point functionality figure is carried as printed, not interpreted as a restored network."
   ],
